4.10.6 The control of corrosion in avionic systems is similar to that in airframes, with 
modifications. Factors affecting corrosion control in avionic equipment include: 
• Less durable protection systems; 
• Small amounts of corrosion can make equipment inoperative; 
• Dissimilar metals are often in electrical contact; 
• Stray currents can cause corrosion; 
• Active metals and dissimilar metals in contact are often unprotected; 
• Closed boxes can produce condensation during normal temperature changes during 
flight; 
